# pubsub2 — SUBSCRIBE versus PSUBSCRIBE
#
# Learn: SUBSCRIBE takes exact channel names. PSUBSCRIBE takes glob-style
# patterns (orders:*, user:?:events) and delivers "pmessage" replies that
# also say which channel matched. Once a connection subscribes, it can
# only run (P)SUBSCRIBE, (P)UNSUBSCRIBE, PING and QUIT.
#
# Task: listen to order events of EVERY region: orders:eu, orders:us and
# any region added later, but not payments:*. The check keeps this
# connection open and publishes to a few channels.
#
# Try it: redislings server; in one terminal `redis-cli -p 6390`, paste
# your command; in another `redis-cli -p 6390 PUBLISH orders:eu hi`.
#

SUBSCRIBE orders:*
